  "syns": [
   {
    "pl": "synonyms",
    "pt": [
     [
      "text",
      "{sc}abandon{/sc} {sc}desert{/sc} {sc}forsake{/sc} mean to leave without intending to return. {sc}abandon{/sc} suggests that the thing or person left may be helpless without protection. "
     ],
     [
      "vis",
      [
       {
        "t": "{it}abandoned{/it} children"
       }
      ]
     ],
     [
      "text",
      " {sc}desert{/sc} implies that the object left may be weakened but not destroyed by one's absence. "
     ],
     [
      "vis",
      [
       {
        "t": "a {it}deserted{/it} town"
       }
      ]
     ],
     [
      "text",
      " {sc}forsake{/sc} suggests an action more likely to bring impoverishment or bereavement to that which is forsaken than its exposure to physical dangers. "
     ],
     [
      "vis",
      [
       {
        "t": "a {it}forsaken{/it} lover"
       }
      ]
     ]
    ],
    "sarefs": [
     "relinquish"
    ]
   }
  ],
  "et": [
   [
    "text",
    "Middle English {it}abandounen{/it}, borrowed from Anglo-French {it}abanduner{/it}, derivative of {it}abandun{/it} \"surrender, abandonment,\" from the phrase {it}a bandun{/it} \"in one's power, at one's disposal,\" from {it}a{/it} \"at, to\" (going back to Latin {it}ad{/it} \"to\") + {it}bandun{/it} \"jurisdiction,\" going back to a Gallo-Romance derivative of Old Low Franconian {it}*bann-{/it} \"summons, command\" (with {it}-d-{/it} probably from outcomes of Germanic {it}*bandwō{/it} \"sign\") {ma}{mat|at:1|}, {mat|ban:1|}, {mat|banner:1|}{/ma}"
   ]
  ],
  "date": "14th century{ds||1|b|}",
  "shortdef": [
